meta {
  name: 01 List Reports
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports?status=PENDING
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  status: PENDING
  ~source: IN_HOUSE
  ~search:
  ~dateFrom:
  ~dateTo:
  ~branchId: {{branchId}}
  ~referredByDoctorId: {{referredByDoctorId}}
  ~referralPanelId: {{referralPanelId}}
  ~departmentId: {{departmentId}}
  ~branchLabPanelId: {{branchLabPanelId}}
  ~branchLabTestId: {{branchLabTestId}}
  ~orderId: {{orderId}}
  ~sampleStatus: COLLECTED
  ~outsource: true
  ~urgent: true
  ~homeCollection: true
  ~page: 1
  ~limit: 25
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  const rows = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data && res.getBody().data.rows;
  if (rows && rows.length) bru.setEnvVar("labReportId", rows[0].id);
}

docs {
  Reporting Worklist (LABORATORY.docx §1.1, §3, §6). Tenant comes from the
  JWT. `status` selects one of the 9 status tabs (omit for All).

  Query params: `status`, `branchId` ("All Branches" filter — explicit value
  overrides the caller's own active branch, same permissive pattern as
  `GET /orders`; omit to default to the caller's active branch), `source`
  (`ALL`|`IN_HOUSE`|`OUTSOURCE`), `search`, `dateFrom`/`dateTo`,
  `referredByDoctorId`, `referralPanelId`, `departmentId`, `branchLabPanelId`,
  `branchLabTestId`, `orderId`, `sampleStatus`, `outsource`, `urgent`,
  `homeCollection`, `page`/`limit` (default 25).

  `orderId` narrows to a single order's reports **regardless of status** (via
  `OrderItem.orderId`) — used by the Patient Entry modal to load every test of
  the selected order (the status tabs only ever load one status at a time). Pair
  with a high `limit` to get the whole order in one page.

  `search` matches Patient Name (first/last), Order ID (order code), Test
  Name (the order item's branch lab test name), or Ref Panel (the order's
  referral panel name) — a hit on any one field matches (substring,
  case-insensitive), independent of the other filters above.

  `sampleStatus` is `NOT_COLLECTED` | `COLLECTED` only — Accession's own
  New/Collected/Accepted/... sample lifecycle doesn't exist in the backend
  yet, so this maps directly to whether `OrderItem.collectedAt` is set (a
  two-state proxy, not the full lifecycle the frontend chip set implies).

  `outsource` is the standalone "Outsource" checkbox. Distinct from the `source`
  pill — it is a SUPERSET, matching `LabReport.isReferral` (not `isOutsourced`).
  It narrows to referral/transfer work from the caller's branch perspective:
  outsourced-out items (same as `source=OUTSOURCE`) PLUS samples that reached
  ACCEPTED through a transfer — the INTERNAL clone received at this branch
  (/accession/referral-orders) and the sender's own report once an EXTERNAL or
  OUTSOURCE transfer is accepted (/accession/external-referral-orders,
  /accession/outsource). `isReferral` is stamped at transfer-accept time, so a
  forwarded/received sample only appears once the receiving/outside party has
  taken it (not while still in transit). The `source` pill stays strict
  (`isOutsourced` = outsource-center only).

  `homeCollection` matches `true` when the order's `OrderDiagnostics.isHomeVisit`
  flag is set — a booking-level home-visit/phlebotomist-collection flag on the
  whole Order (joined through `OrderItem.order.diagnostics`), distinct from
  anything on `OrderItem`/`LabReport` itself.

  TAT alert pills (Warning/Critical/Imminent/Breached) are explicitly out of
  scope per LABORATORY.docx — not a filter here.

  **Branch columns (per row).** `branch` / `branchId` are the branch that
  HOLDS the report — after an internal transfer (Sent Internal) the one report
  row moves to the receiving branch, and every caller sees the same `branch`.
  `displayBranch` (`{ id, name }`, or `null`) is what the Branch column shows for
  THIS caller: where the caller's own sample came from — the branch that SENT the
  caller's copy of the sample, or the caller's own branch when it holds the
  original. For a report that goes A → B → C: A's row shows A, B's row shows A,
  C's row shows B (while `branch` is C for all three). It is `null` when none of
  the caller's branches holds a linked sample (the screen then shows `branch`);
  with "All Branches", the sample held by the report's holder decides. Permissions
  and scoping always use `branchId`, never `displayBranch`.

  Returns `{ rows, total, page, limit }`. Captures `labReportId` from the
  first row for the requests below. 422 `ACTIVE_BRANCH_REQUIRED` if the
  caller has no active branch.

  **Department visibility is per branch (Phase 2).** A report is visible when the department of the entry the viewing
  branch works the test with is unassigned or one of the caller's departments: for a report the branch HOLDS that is
  its own entry once the report was sent to it (`performingBranchLabTestId`), otherwise the order line's; for a report
  the branch only SENT (the sender view) it is the order line's entry. The row's `departmentId` is the department of
  the holding branch's entry.
}
